  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Ritual songs of the Midewiwin, the Grand Medicine Society of the Ojibwe, Menominee, Potawatomi and other Great Lakes peoples, sung in the society's initiation and healing ceremonies and recorded on wax cylinder from Mide singers in Minnesota in the early twentieth century. Mide songs were remembered with the help of pictographs incised on birchbark scrolls, and are accompanied by the Mide water drum and rattles. A hand-drum card stands in for the water drum and a generic shaker card for the rattles.",
